<id/00/0093/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Oars"@en ;
    skos:broadMatch <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300213077>, <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2003749> ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_cooperage_ship_timber/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "(GER. *Riemen* (zu *fahreugen*). DU. *Riemen*. DA. *Aarer*. SW. *Avor*. FR. *Avirons*, *Rames*. IT. *Remi*. SP. and PORT. *Remos*.) Oar, in navigation, a long piece of wood, for moving a vessel by rowing. Oars for ships are generally cut out of fir-timber, those for barges are made out of New England or Dantzic rafters, and those for boats out of English ash, or Norway fir-rafters. [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 678]"@en ;
